{"path":"experimental/future","title":"std::experimental::future","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::</span>future","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/future","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The class template std::experimental::future extends std::future with the following operations:","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code>&lt;experimental/future&gt;</code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-concurrency\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> future<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-concurrency-ts t-mark-ts\">(concurrency TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-concurrency\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> future<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-concurrency-ts t-mark-ts\">(concurrency TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-concurrency\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> future<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-concurrency-ts t-mark-ts\">(concurrency TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The class template <code>std::experimental::future</code> extends <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future\">std::future</a></span> with the following operations:\n</p>\n<ul><li> an <i>unwrapping constructor</i> from <code>future&lt;future&lt;T&gt;&gt;</code>;\n</li><li> a member function <code>is_ready</code> to query whether the associated shared state is ready; and\n</li><li> a member function <code>then</code> to attach a continuation to the future.\n</li></ul>\n<p>However, there is no interoperation between <code>std::experimental::future</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future\">std::future</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/future/future\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  construct a <code>future</code> object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/future/is_ready\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_ready</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the shared state is ready <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/future/then\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>then</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  attaches a continuation to a future <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/future/operator=\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator=</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  moves the future object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div id=\"identical-\" data-bg=\"e3f9df\">\n<h2 id=\"Members_identical_to_std::future\">Members  identical to std::future </h2>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions_2\">Member functions</h3>\n<p>Note that <code>share()</code> returns a <span class=\"t-lc\">std::experimental::shared_future&lt;T&gt;</span>. The behavior is otherwise identical.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/~future\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(destructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  destructs the future object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/share\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>share</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  transfers the shared state from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> to a <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/shared_future\"><code>shared_future</code></a> and returns it <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <h5 id=\"Getting_the_result\">Getting the result </h5>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/get\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>get</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the result <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <h5 id=\"State\">State </h5>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/valid\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>valid</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the future has a shared state <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/wait\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wait</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  waits for the result to become available <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/wait_for\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wait_for</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  waits for the result, returns if it is not available for the specified timeout duration <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future/wait_until\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wait_until</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  waits for the result, returns if it is not available until specified time point has been reached <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/shared_future\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>shared_future</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-concurrency-ts t-mark-ts\">(concurrency TS)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  a version of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/shared_future\">std::shared_future</a></span> enhanced with continuations and other features <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":2,"text":"Members identical to std::future","id":"Members_identical_to_std::future"},{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions_2"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"}],"children":[{"path":"experimental/future/future","title":"std::experimental::future<T>::future"},{"path":"experimental/future/is_ready","title":"std::experimental::future<T>::is_ready"},{"path":"experimental/future/operator=","title":"std::experimental::future<T>::operator="},{"path":"experimental/future/then","title":"std::experimental::future<T>::then"}],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::future","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations. The class template std::experimental::future extends std::future with the following operations:"},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"construct a future object"},{"label":"is_ready","note":"checks if the shared state is ready"},{"label":"then","note":"attaches a continuation to a future"},{"label":"operator=","note":"moves the future object"}]},{"label":"Members identical to std::future","note":"Note that share() returns a std::experimental::shared_future<T>. The behavior is otherwise identical.","children":[{"label":"Member functions","note":"Note that share() returns a std::experimental::shared_future<T>. The behavior is otherwise identical."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":268,"codeBlockCount":0}
